    "sensesNotes": "Darkvision 120 ft., Keen Smell",
    "tactics": "Swamp Cats hunt in pairs or small groups, using the terrain to stalk prey before committing to Pounce. Pack Tactics and Pounce together make their opening turn devastating — one cat charges to trigger Prone while the second attacks with subtracted dice against the downed target. They break off if badly wounded, retreating into the swamp to recover.\n \n---",
    "attacksNotes": "<p><strong>Bite [Combat]:</strong> Melee attack (Agil 4 + Melee Combat 5), Reach 5 ft.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><em>Margin 1:</strong></em> 10 damage (Large, standard natural weapon: 8 + 2)</li>\n<li><strong><em>Margin 2:</strong></em> 15 damage (10 + 5 Str)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Claw [Combat]:</strong> Melee attack (Agil 4 + Melee Combat 5), Reach 5 ft.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><em>Margin 1:</strong></em> 10 damage (Large, standard natural weapon: 8 + 2)</li>\n<li><strong><em>Margin 2:</strong></em> 15 damage (10 + 5 Str)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Multiattack [Combat]:</strong> The Swamp Cat makes one bite and one claw attack.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong><em>Shared Attribute Roll (Agil 4):</strong></em> Roll once, apply to both attacks. Roll Melee Combat skill die separately for each.</li>\n</ul>",
    "specialAbilitiesNotes": "<p><strong>Keen Smell:</strong> Scent-based Perception checks have Fortune.</p>\n<p><strong>Pack Tactics:</strong> When an ally is within 5 feet of the target, subtract 1 from both attack dice.</p>\n<p><strong>Pounce:</strong> If the Swamp Cat moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits with a claw attack on the same turn, the target must make a Fortitude save (Con + Luck, opposed by the Cat's Str 5 + Melee Combat 5). On failure, the target gains the Prone condition. If the target is Prone, the Swamp Cat may immediately make one bite attack against it as a [Free] action.</p>",
